  "group": "Calendar",
  "title": "Calendar",
  "adapter": "calendar",
  "viewports": ["pro-max"],
  "note": "MainCalendar (tab root). The iPhone reference renders the TOP of the month window (today −12 months) because the harness snapshot precedes the controller's scroll-to-current-month — so `default` seeds the window start, where no dots/today disc are visible, matching it. `today` is pinned to the iPhone capture date (2026-06-29) so both sides stay deterministic. `with-events` (dots + today disc + selection ring) and `expanded` (the curtain-split event list, which is internal UIKit state the harness cannot reach) are WEB-ONLY: making them two-sided needs a re-capture with a scrolled/seeded controller.",
